{"myopic":{"id":"452e20bc-1d25-442e-b695-e675b1d5bf99","word":"myopic","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"unable to see distant objects unaided","word":"míope"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"unable to see distant objects unaided","word":"miópico"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Corrective lenses compensate for the excessive positive diopters of the myopic eye.","bold_text_offsets":[[72,78]],"type":"example","id":"8652351c-d820-419e-8389-8d6d7accf55b"},{"text":"A stronger prescription for myopic night drivers is often needed.","bold_text_offsets":[[28,34]],"type":"example","id":"cd899e37-4599-44c7-be43-b78c7311485e"},{"text":"She yanked the paper from her motherʼs hands, bringing it very close to her myopic eyes.","ref":"2005, Zadie Smith, On Beauty, Penguin Books (2006), page 13:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[76,82]],"id":"31bf9238-a72e-4aa3-a2ba-e0e2536e0480"}],"links":[["Near-sighted","near-sighted"],["distant","distant"],["object","object"],["unaided","unaided"]],"antonyms":[{"word":"hyperopic"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["Near-sighted; unable to see distant objects unaided."],"id":"3e56cdeb-75b0-4115-a166-eede15b0d668"},{"examples":[{"text":"The real problem, he insists, is the myopic mentality that has failed to address climate change to date. The rich world’s indifference to the despoliation of the environment in pursuit of short-term economic gain is rooted in a wider problem.","ref":"2015 June 28, Paul Vallely, “The Pope's Ecological Vow”, in The New York Times, →ISSN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[37,43]],"id":"699e3ea4-8c91-4993-8a4f-2f8f5c901b87"},{"text":"His postwar roles, full of myopic obsession, stalkerish derangement, and a desire for vengeance, don't seem like ground Hanks is willing to cover.","ref":"2021 February 9, Christina Newland, “Is Tom Hanks part of a dying breed